==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|straungely|t=strangely, aloofly, intricately}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|strange|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɹeɪndʒli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-strangely.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[strange]] or [[coincidental]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|Though I'd never gone to Boston before, everything looked '''strangely''' familiar.}}
#: {{ux|en|Daniel was walking '''strangely''' because he had twisted his ankle.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Surprisingly, wonderfully.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest||4|1|text={{...}}all thy vexations / Were but my trials of thy love, and thou / Hast '''strangely''' stood the test{{...}}}}

